Subject: [PATCH 03496/11362] [outer-loop] Fold verifier-as-Q-head arc into
 .425 + flag SpatialValueNet routing upgrade

(1) .425 known-issues fold now carries the full verifier-as-Q-head arc (v1->v5): the learned value
is the session's one genuine positive -- a position-aware SpatialValueNet routes ls20-L1 7.6x faster
than blind (the dense gradient every hand/LLM goal lacked), but it's per-level (does not deepen; L2
is gradient-bound) and game-dependent (7.6x clean-nav, ~1.2x elsewhere).
(2) Flagged the SHIPPABLE upgrade: wire SpatialValueNet + tuned heuristic_weight into the conductor's
arc_loop_solve, replacing the linear LearnedVerifier we've shown cannot route. Per-level routing
speedup on navigation games (faster banking, not deeper levels).

Conductor left stopped (operator chose 1+2, not restart). Changelog updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
